🧠 Introduction

Modern AI models (LLMs) like GPT are powerful because of:

* Large number of parameters
* Scaling laws
* High training compute

👉 These concepts explain **why bigger models perform better**.

----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

🔢 1. What are Parameters?

Parameters are the **learnable weights inside a model**.

👉 They store knowledge learned during training.

---

📌 Example

```text id="q3m7kp"
y = wx + b
```

Here:

* w → weight (parameter)
* b → bias (parameter)

---

🔹 In Neural Networks

* Each connection has weights
* Millions to billions of parameters

---

📊 Examples of Model Sizes

| Model               | Parameters  |
| ------------------- | ----------- |
| Small ML Model      | Thousands   |
| Deep Learning Model | Millions    |
| GPT-3               | 175 Billion |
| GPT-4/5             | Even larger |

---

🎯 Why Parameters Matter?

✔ More parameters → more learning capacity
✔ Better pattern recognition
✔ Improved accuracy

---

⚠️ Limitation

❌ Too many parameters → overfitting
❌ Requires more compute
❌ Expensive to train

----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

📈 2. Scaling Laws

Scaling laws describe how model performance improves with:

* Model size
* Data size
* Compute

---

🔹 Key Idea

```text id="x7k4pz"
Performance improves as we increase model, data, and compute
```

---

📊 Scaling Factors

1️⃣ Model Size (Parameters)
2️⃣ Dataset Size
3️⃣ Training Compute

---

📉 Graph Insight (Concept)

As we increase:

* Parameters ↑
* Data ↑
* Compute ↑

👉 Error decreases (better performance)

---

🔥 Important Observation

✔ Larger models perform better
✔ More data improves generalization
✔ Compute enables training large models

-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

⚡ 3. Training Compute

Training compute refers to **computational resources used to train models**.

---

🔹 What Includes Compute?

* GPUs / TPUs
* Memory
* Training time
* Energy consumption

---

📊 Example

Training large models like GPT requires:

* Thousands of GPUs
* Weeks or months of training
* Huge cost

---

🔹 Compute Formula (Concept)

```text id="p8m2qx"
Compute ∝ Parameters × Data × Training Steps
```

----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

💰 Challenges of High Compute

❌ Expensive
❌ Requires infrastructure
❌ Energy consumption
❌ Limited accessibility

---

🔗 Connection Between Concepts

| Concept      | Role                    |
| ------------ | ----------------------- |
| Parameters   | Model capacity          |
| Scaling Laws | Performance improvement |
| Compute      | Enables training        |

